course: dictionary
lesson: 4776
title: Informal words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are informal. People use them when they chat with friends and family, not in school essays or letters to the bank. Hubby is one of these words. It is a short, friendly way of saying husband. «My hubby is making pancakes this morning» sounds warm and relaxed.
explain: Look at how the word is used to find its feeling. Hubby sounds loving and a bit joking, so it is not the same as the formal word husband. Ask yourself who is speaking and who they are speaking to. In a story, a character who says «my hubby» is usually chatty and warm.
explain: Hubby is a noun, and its plural is hubbies. You can say the hubby or my hubby. «My other half» and «my partner» can also mean someone's husband, but those words can mean a husband, wife or partner, so they are wider than hubby.
fact: Hubby is an informal noun meaning husband.
fact: Hubby is said in a friendly, joking or loving way.
fact: The plural of hubby is hubbies.
fact: «My hubby» and «the hubby» are common phrases in casual speech.
fact: Informal words suit chatting and messages, but they are less suitable for formal writing.
exercise: «My hubby drove us to the beach.» What does hubby mean? | A bus driver | A holiday | *A husband | A neighbour
exercise: Mum texts her friend: «Hubby is cooking tea tonight.» Who is cooking? | The next-door neighbour | *Mum's husband | Her dog | The teacher at school
exercise: Which word is best for a formal letter to the bank about your husband? | Other half | Hubbies | Hubby | *Husband
test: What is the plural of hubby? | Hubbis | Hubbys | Hubby's | *Hubbies
test: A friend asks, «Is your husband coming?» Which reply sounds most like a chatty friend? | «Affirmative, my spouse arrives shortly.» | *«Yeah, my hubby's on his way!» | «Hubby is a noun.» | «My husband has been informed.»
exam: In a story, Ella says, «My hubby says we should walk home.» What does the word hubby tell you about Ella? | She is cold and very formal | She has never met her husband | She is giving a maths lesson | *She is warm, friendly and chatty
